8) SCALING BOTTLENECKS — SENIOR ENGINEER THINKING
==============================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
BOTTLENECK 1: LOCK HOLD TIME
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prepared transactions hold locks till phase 2.

Causes:
- contention
- deadlocks
- poor throughput

High write systems suffer badly:
- payments
- inventory
- wallet ledgers

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
BOTTLENECK 2: COORDINATOR HOTSPOT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Single coordinator handles:
- state machine
- retries
- timeouts
- logging

Scaling solution:
- partition by txn_id hash
- multiple coordinators
- leader per shard

Tradeoff:
cross-shard observability harder.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
BOTTLENECK 3: CROSS-REGION LATENCY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 RTT minimum + disk flush.

Rough:
- local region: manageable
- multi-region: expensive

Hence:
Google Spanner uses consensus-backed commit instead of naive 2PC alone.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
BOTTLENECK 4: LONG RUNNING TRANSACTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Never use 2PC for:
- hotel booking workflow
- food delivery driver matching
- 30 min payment timeout
- async human approvals

Use Saga instead.

==============================================================================
9) CONSISTENCY + REPLICATION + FAILOVER THINKING
==============================================================================

REPLICATION MODEL
Coordinator log should be replicated.

WHY
Coordinator crash otherwise blocks system.

Best practice:
Raft replicated WAL.

FAILOVER
Standby coordinator reads replicated log and resumes:
- commit retries
- abort retries
- participant reconciliation

QUORUM ROLE
If coordinator state is quorum replicated:
- failover safe
- no split-brain decisions

CONSISTENCY GUARANTEE
Strong atomic commit guarantee
BUT only if coordinator durable state survives.

Important nuance:
2PC itself is atomic commit protocol,
NOT full replication protocol.

==============================================================================
10) ALTERNATIVES + TRADEOFFS
==============================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
A) SAGA PATTERN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY
For microservices and long workflows.

Instead of locks:
- local commits
- compensating rollback actions

Example:
Uber Eats order
- payment
- restaurant accept
- driver assign
- compensate if failed

Tradeoff:
eventual consistency
harder compensation logic

Use when:
availability > strict atomicity

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
B) OUTBOX + EVENT DRIVEN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Use for:
DB write + Kafka publish consistency.

Better for:
Instagram notifications
WhatsApp message fanout
analytics pipelines

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
C) CONSENSUS COMMIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Used in:
Google Spanner
CockroachDB

Why better:
non-blocking under coordinator failover

Tradeoff:
higher complexity

